body.translated_text:
It is cooling, bestows complexion and strength, is sweet, <s>vṛṣya</s> (aphrodisiac), and binding;
it removes <s>vāta</s> (wind), eliminates <s>kapha</s> (phlegm), promotes taste, is <s>hṛdya</s> (cardiac tonic), and removes all three <s>doṣas</s> (humors) (alleviates pain in all limbs);
it gives relief from cough, fatigue from travel, promotes desire, bestows radiance, and is nourishing.

With alkaline properties, it removes <s>kapha</s> (phlegm), <s>pitta</s> (bile), and <s>vāta</s> (wind), stimulates the digestive fire and loosens the bowels;
bitter, hot, and sweet, also pungent in taste, and slightly aggravating <s>pitta</s> (bile);
<s>hṛdya</s> (cordial), not causing <s>vāta</s> (wind) disorders, not unwholesome with wine, but among all substances again
(cordial, appetizing, not aggravating <s>pitta</s>, and subduing <s>kapha</s> — the best of all vegetables),
